<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 269 0 R
/E (Improvements:  A future offseason goal is to increase the hopper capacity to about 50 fuel while maintaining reliable ball movement. We also plan to design a more integrated hopper and intake subsystem to improve efficiency and control fuel flow. Additionally, making the hopper less wide could create enough space on the robot to include a climbing mechanism while still maintaining a large-capacity fuel storage system.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 271 0 R
/E (Strength: The extendable hopper improves scoring efficiency by allowing the robot to store a larger amount of fuel before returning to score. By expanding during collection, the drive team can spend less time traveling between zones. The design also helps keep fuel moving through the system, especially with the added agitator and hopper movement, which improves ball flow and supports more consistent shooting performance.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 272 0 R
/E (Weakness:  During initial prototype testing, we discovered that two balls could become stuck at the same time, causing jams in the hopper. This required adjustments to the design, including adding an agitator and using hopper movement to keep the fuel in motion. The extendable design also required us to prioritize space for the hopper, which meant we chose not to include a climbing mechanism on the robot.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
